# Native agent-device action sections; suite.json composes guards and includes.
# settings-font

# section open-settings
press "${TARGET}"

# section settings-arrived
is visible "${TARGET}"

# section open-font
# The Font row is in APPEARANCE, the second card on the page, so it is on
# screen when Settings arrives and needs no seek. It is also above the `deep`
# fold (`settings.tsx`), which is why this flow can reach it on the frame the
# push finishes rather than waiting for the idle callback the ABOUT rows need.
press "${TARGET}"

# section sheet-arrived
wait stable 400 5000

# section group-visible
# Both group headings, which is the whole shape of the sheet: two slots that
# answer different questions. A sheet that lost one of them would still open,
# still show a current face, and silently have stopped offering the other half
# of the feature -- so the headings are what is asserted rather than the rows.
is visible "${TARGET}"

# section row-visible
# The way back to the platform's own face, in both groups. It is the one
# control on this sheet that must never be missing: everything else here adds
# a font, and this is the only thing that undoes it. Asserted and not pressed,
# because the flow runs on a shared QA device in demo mode with no font
# installed -- there is nothing to undo, and the row says so by being disabled.
is visible "${TARGET}"

# section leave
# Android's back dismisses a form sheet, which is the same gesture a reader
# has. The grabber and the swipe are the close; there is no X to press.
back --system

# section back-on-settings
is visible "${TARGET}"
